"          answer before submission."
msgstr ""
"Yes. The system reads back your typed response using text-to-speech. You can "
"review, edit, and\n"
"          confirm your\n"
"          answer before submission."

#: templates/index.html:340
msgid "How do I answer questions?"
msgstr "How do I answer questions?"

#: templates/index.html:342
msgid ""
"You listen to the question through headphones and speak your answer clearly "
"into a microphone.\n"
"          The system\n"
"          converts your speech into text instantly."
msgstr ""
"You listen to the question through headphones and speak your answer clearly "
"into a microphone.\n"
"          The system\n"
"          converts your speech into text instantly."

#: templates/index.html:350
msgid "Do I need computer skills to use it?"
msgstr "Do I need computer skills to use it?"

#: templates/index.html:352
msgid ""
"No. The interface is simple and guided. Minimal training is required before "
"the\n"
"          exam."
msgstr ""
"No. The interface is simple and guided. Minimal training is required before "
"the\n"
"          exam."

#: templates/index.html:359
msgid "What infrastructure is required?"
msgstr "What infrastructure is required?"

#: templates/index.html:361
msgid ""
"Standard computers or laptops with headsets and microphones are sufficient. "
"For large-scale\n"
"          deployment,\n"
"          dedicated ASR/TTS server configurations can be implemented."
msgstr ""
"Standard computers or laptops with headsets and microphones are sufficient. "
"For large-scale\n"
"          deployment,\n"
"          dedicated ASR/TTS server configurations can be implemented."

#: templates/index.html:369
msgid "Can it reduce administrative burden?"
msgstr "Can it reduce administrative burden?"

#: templates/index.html:371
msgid ""
"Yes. It eliminates scribe management, reduces approval delays, and "
"standardizes accommodation\n"
"          processes."
msgstr ""
"Yes. It eliminates scribe management, reduces approval delays, and "
"standardizes accommodation\n"
"          processes."

#: templates/index.html:378
msgid "How secure is the system?"
msgstr "How secure is the system?"

#: templates/index.html:380
msgid ""
"The system operates in a controlled examination environment with secure "
"recording, answer\n"
"          storage, and audit\n"
"          capability to maintain academic integrity."
msgstr ""
"The system operates in a controlled examination environment with secure "
"recording, answer\n"
"          storage, and audit\n"
"          capability to maintain academic integrity."

#: templates/index.html:393
msgid "What institutions say"
msgstr "What institutions say"

#: templates/index.html:399
msgid ""
"Today we had an Academic Audit visit (inspection) in our college. Happy to\n"
"          share with you\n"
"          that Voice-based software / examination initiative is very "
"appreciated by all expert team members. Then we\n"
"          were asked for some clarification and we successfully answered all "
"queries. Thank you so much for your\n"
"          contribution towards the upliftment of students."
msgstr ""
"Today we had an Academic Audit visit (inspection) in our college. Happy to\n"
"          share with you\n"
"          that Voice-based software / examination initiative is very "
"appreciated by all expert team members. Then we\n"
"          were asked for some clarification and we successfully answered all "
"queries. Thank you so much for your\n"
"          contribution towards the upliftment of students."

#: templates/index.html:404
msgid "Exam Coordinator, College XX"
msgstr "Exam Coordinator, College XX"

#: templates/index.html:408
msgid ""
"This is to inform you that testing is completed successfully for the\n"
"          ‘Examination System for\n"
"          Visually/Physically Impaired People’ at our end. We will connect "
"soon for further\n"
"          processing."
msgstr ""
"This is to inform you that testing is completed successfully for the\n"
"          ‘Examination System for\n"
"          Visually/Physically Impaired People’ at our end. We will connect "
"soon for further\n"
"          processing."

